{
  "rationale": "The design separates sensing availability from motion capability in the plant and uses small deterministic specifications to map sensed obstacle conditions to exactly one safe exploratory or recovery action. Clear-space behavior is biased toward coverage by making random_walk the default exploration action and inserting a short move_forward progress step after a clear exploratory pulse. Obstacle reactions are conservative: any obstacle event routes through a dedicated turn-recovery state, with left obstacles forcing clockwise recovery, right obstacles forcing counterclockwise recovery, and front obstacles using a dedicated clockwise recovery. Uncontrollable events are total in every specification state, and action/commit states self-loop on non-critical path_clear so intended one-shot actions are not preempted in the same step.",
  "strategy": [
    "Use permissive plant automata: one for sensor events and one for motion commands.",
    "Use one policy specification with small helper states to enforce exactly one controllable action per explore/recovery state and quick return to exploration after path_clear."
  ],
